WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.920
Marvel didn't wait too long to give us our
first look at the upcoming ​The Eternals.​

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:08.760
Concept art for the flick, which will be the
second film in the MCU's Phase 4, was recently

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:09.770
released online.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.930
It depicts a quartet of the ancient beings
known as Celestials walking across the surface

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:14.680
of a barren planet.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.420
We've been introduced to these beings just
a couple of times before, once in each of

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.119
the Guardians of the Galaxy movies.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:24.599
In Guardians Vol. 1, our heroes traveled to
the mining colony of Exitar to meet with The

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:27.869
Collector, who had some knowledge to impart
about the Infinity Stones.

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:31.520
Exitar is situated within Knowhere, which
is actually the severed head of a deceased

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:32.020
Celestial.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.940
A later scene also seemed to showcase a look
at a Celestial as it uses the Power Stone

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.380
to effortlessly destroy an entire planet.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:47.540
“These powerful carriers can destroy entire
civilizations like wheat in a field.”

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:52.470
In Guardians Vol. 2, we got our first proper
introduction to one of the all-powerful entities

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:57.170
in the form of Ego, the "Living Planet," who
was revealed to be the father of Peter Quill.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:00.910
Ego didn't look a lot like the Celestials
pictured, but we can assume that Celestials

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.300
come in all shapes and sizes.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.400
Plus, we can assume from Ego's ability to
masquerade as a human that Celestials can

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.860
also assume other forms if need be.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.510
In Marvel lore, the Celestials existed before
virtually any other form of sentient life

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:13.340
in the universe.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:18.060
Millions of years ago, they were responsible
for the creation of the Eternals — near-immortal,

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.180
superpowered humanoids — and their polar
opposite race, the Deviants, which are essentially

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.540
the Eternal equivalent of mutants.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:27.640
The two races have been locked in struggle
for centuries, with the Eternals tasked with

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:29.940
defending Earth from the Deviants' conquest.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:34.500
Thus far in the MCU, we haven't met any Eternals
that we know of, but we have met one Deviant.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.520
Thanos, the Mad Titan who embarked on a quest
to collect all six Infinity Stones and wipe

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
out half of all life in the universe, carries
the Deviant gene in Marvel comics.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.980
It's not yet known to what extent the Celestials
will figure into the narrative of The Eternals;

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:51.200
Marvel’s head honcho Kevin Feige has hinted
that the flick could be an epic spanning tens

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.250
of thousands of years, so we may only get
a look at them in the form of some exposition

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.800
on the ancient history of the universe.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:59.980
As for the Eternals themselves, we at least
have an idea of what the team that will be

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:04.360
featured in the movie will look like, thanks
to Marvel's recent panel at San Diego Comic-Con

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:04.920
2019.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:09.899
The entire primary cast was announced at the
event, and it includes Richard Madden as Ikaris,

00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:14.260
the leader of the flick's team of heroes;
Angelina Jolie as Thena, also known as Azura,

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:18.950
who in the comics has been known to consort
with Deviants; Kumail Nanjiani as Kingo, who

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:22.840
took up residence in Japan thousands of years
ago and learned the ways of the Samurai; Lauren

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:28.460
Ridloff as Makkari, an expert mechanical engineer
and speedster; Brian Tyree Henry as Phastos,

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:33.100
a master weapons-smith; Salma Hayek as Ajak,
who has spent most of her thousands of Earthly

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:37.880
years in Siberia; finally young Lia McHugh
as Sprite, a trickster who is forever stuck

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.820
with the appearance of a pre-teen child.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:43.940
The Eternals begins shooting next month, so
hopefully, it won't be too long before some

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.420
unofficial set photos of the stars in costume
arrive.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:50.500
Of course, there will probably be plenty more
of these interesting little hints and revelations

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:53.620
that will come trickling out in the wake of
Marvel's epic Comic-Con panel.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.480
We'll keep our eye out for them, and keep
you up to date.

